      "A Sri Lanka CV format asks for more personal detail than a Western resume and it expects that detail in a set order. Many employers still look for a religion line and a national identity card number and a date of birth and two named referees with working phone numbers. Presentation carries real weight here and a tidy complete document signals a careful applicant. The format rewards patience because every expected line on the page has a practical reason behind it. Recently updated.",
